WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.550
This is TrueSite: the design, standing where you build it.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.883
On site, crews build without the model in front of them.

3
00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:14.017
In one industry survey, team members lost 14 hours a week to hunting for data, conflicts and rework.

4
00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:18.150
Almost half of all rework came from miscommunication and poor project data.

5
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:24.050
TrueSite starts with a printed QR code at a surveyed spot.

6
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:29.750
Scan it with the phone’s camera and TrueSite opens in the browser. Nothing to install.

7
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.150
Ten seconds of tilting calibrates the camera.

8
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.350
The code’s corners give the pose; the motion sensors hold the model steady and level.

9
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:47.750
Now the building stands at life size, where it will be built.

10
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:54.950
Turn around, look up: it stays put over the real ground.

11
00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:06.550
Tap any element to see what it is, its size and its material, straight from the BIM model.

12
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:15.450
The same building at 1:100 on a desk.

13
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:24.150
Ask Gemini about any element: it answers only from that element’s own model data, and shows the fields it used.

14
00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:32.246
Our building isn’t built yet, so judges can step into a simulated as-built site with ten defects planted on purpose.

15
00:01:32.296 --> 00:01:40.142
Tap Check as-built. Gemini compares three images: your view, the design render with numbered marks, and each element’s design outline.

16
00:01:40.192 --> 00:01:48.038
Findings are pinned on the view and scored against what was planted: what Gemini caught and what it missed.

17
00:01:48.088 --> 00:01:55.934
Severity and “Why it matters” come from fixed rules, not the model. Every finding is a visual check, not a survey.

18
00:01:55.984 --> 00:02:03.830
Gemini drafts the issue in the crew’s language; a person edits and saves it.

19
00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:11.430
In the office, the 3D model shows the same findings, saved issues and Ask Gemini.

20
00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:18.830
Pose, sensor fusion and rendering run on the phone.

21
00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:26.030
Cloud Run serves the app and the API; Gemini 3.8 Flash on Agent Platform does the judging; Firestore and Cloud Storage keep the records. A check costs about US$0.015.

22
00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:33.430
TrueSite helps contractors catch mistakes before they’re poured in concrete: less rework, faster sign-off, safer sites.

23
00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:40.630
Try it at truesite-1067044308557.asia-southeast1.run.app. The code is at github.com/wl-geek/truesite.
